; range_empty_unmatched: an empty RANGE whose body has no NEXT raises
; UNMATCHED_LOOP.
;
; A non-positive count skips the body by scanning forward for the matching
; NEXT (spec/xqvm/ISA.md's empty-loop skip clause). Running off the end of
; the stream instead means the loop was never closed, which
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md:196 gives its own identity -- distinct from the
; NO_ACTIVE_LOOP a stray NEXT raises. The pair is the reason xqvm_py's
; single LoopError class had to be split (QUI-1289).

PUSH 0
PUSH 0
RANGE          ; loop [0, 0) -- empty, so the body is skipped
PUSH 99
HALT
